Notes / recommendations
- fcntl locks are advisory — every writer must use them. Your server threads do, so this works internally. If other processes write the same files, they must also use locks.
- You should still use your sentence-level locks (lock_sentence_ss) to serialize logical edits at a sentence granularity; the fcntl file lock prevents races at the filesystem level while you parse/modify/write.
- Performance: repeated parse/write is I/O heavy. If you expect many small edits, an in-memory cache + periodic flush or an append/operation log with background compaction would be more efficient.
- Atomicity: writing to a temp file then rename gives you atomic replace semantics on the same filesystem.
- Undo: you already create an undo backup; ensure it is made before the atomic rename.

